All six features implemented and verified.

**`app/auth.py`** — `require_api_key` now raises 401 when the `X-API-Key` header is missing or not in `VALID_API_KEYS`, otherwise returns the mapped username.

**`app/main.py`**:
- `GET /tasks` — optional `status`, `priority`, `assigned_to` filters (combinable), then `page`/`page_size` slicing (defaults 1/20).
- `POST /tasks` — requires auth, 404 if `project_id` not in `projects`, ID auto-generated via `max(id)+1`, returns the created task (201).
- `PUT /tasks/{task_id}` — requires auth, partial updates applied via `model_dump(exclude_unset=True)` so only sent fields change, 404 if not found.
- `DELETE /tasks/{task_id}` — requires auth, removes and returns 204, 404 if not found.

Verified against the challenge validator's contract plus edge cases: **17/17 checks pass** (`_verify.py` ran the exact validator assertions — filter by status/assigned_to, pagination, auth-required on POST, create with unique id, invalid project 404, partial PUT, delete-then-404 — plus priority filter, combined filters, page 2, invalid key, missing-task 404s, and auth on PUT/DELETE).

One design note: mutation endpoints accept either 200/201/204 per the validator, so I used the RESTful defaults (201 create, 204 delete).
